---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase, site } from '../lib/site';
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Doomer Optimism is a pluralistic conversation about how to live well in the age of the Machine. Rooted in Catholic Social Teaching, ecumenical in its conversation, practical in its commitments.">
  <div class="container-prose pt-12 md:pt-20 pb-24">
    <p class="smallcaps mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="mb-6">A clear-eyed, hopeful conversation.</h1>

    <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-umber-100 italic mb-10 leading-snug max-w-prose">
      "How do we live well in the age of the Machine?"
    </p>

    <p class="drop-cap text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200 mb-6">
      Doomer Optimism is a pluralistic conversation hosted by Ashley Colby Fitzgerald —
      sociologist, farmer, mother, and co-founder of <a href="https://rizomafieldschool.com">Rizoma Field School</a>.
      Across more than 300 episodes since 2021, the show has platformed practitioners
      and thinkers who reject both techno-utopian denial and apocalyptic exit, and who
      instead do the patient work of building human-scale alternatives.
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200 mb-6">
      Our intellectual lineage runs through Wendell Berry, Ivan Illich, Christopher Lasch,
      and Morris Berman. Our practical commitments are rooted in <em>Catholic Social
      Teaching</em> — particularly the principles of subsidiarity, solidarity, and
      stewardship — and ecumenical in conversation: Orthodox masons, Protestant farmers,
      secular ecologists, and Jewish urbanists are equally at home in this archive,
      because the work of caring for creation and community does not belong to any
      single tradition.
    </p>

    <PullQuote attribution="The historic labor cry of bread and roses">
      Material sufficiency <em>and</em> beauty.<br />Dignity, creativity, and rooted belonging.
    </PullQuote>

    <h2 class="!text-3xl mt-16 mb-4">What we make</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200 mb-6">
      Each main episode arrives with a full transcript, a categorized bibliography, and a
      1,500–2,500 word companion essay — published here, on
      <a href={site.social.substack}>Substack</a>, on
      <a href={site.social.youtube}>YouTube</a>, and across the major podcast directories.
      The site you are reading is the hub: it holds the searchable archive, the
      bibliography across all episodes, and the long-form research library that turns
      ephemeral conversations into a permanent reference.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-3xl mt-16 mb-4">Six pillars</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200 mb-6">
      The episodes organize around six interlocking arenas:
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/regenerative-agriculture')}>regenerative agriculture</a>,
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/conservation-environment')}>conservation</a>,
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/built-environment')}>the built environment</a>,
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/technology-ai-transhumanism')}>technology &amp; AI</a>,
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/right-to-repair-surveillance')}>right to repair &amp; surveillance</a>, and
      <a href={withBase('/pillars/tech-limited-child-rearing')}>tech-limited child-rearing &amp; schooling</a>.
      Each is anchored by a lead voice and grows its own slow-built reading list.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-3xl mt-16 mb-4">Where we're going</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200 mb-6">
      The next phase: a sustainable cadence of 30–40 episodes per year, the full
      backfilled transcript archive, the launch of the categorized research library, and
      a future think-tank arm that turns the network's collective wisdom into white
      papers and policy briefs. We are moving toward a pattern that resembles the most
      respected independent intellectual platforms — without losing the show's particular,
      rooted voice.
    </p>

    <h2 class="!text-3xl mt-16 mb-4">Brought to you by</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-umber-200">
      The current pilot season is sponsored by <a href={site.sponsor.href}>{site.sponsor.name}</a> —
      a suite of apps embedding Catholic Social Teaching and liturgical rhythm into the
      daily tools of ministries, classical schools, homeschool coops, land trusts, worker
      cooperatives, and walkable neighborhoods.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p class="smallcaps">For partnership and press inquiries: <a href="mailto:ashley@rizomafieldschool.com">ashley@rizomafieldschool.com</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
